speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, we have not had our final discussions with the United States and there may be some slight changes, but as it stands now we expect the qualifications will be as follows.
Registration as a pilot. (1) a person shall not be registered as a pilot by the Canadian Minister of Transport unless:
(a)	he is a Canadian citizen;
(b)	he holds a master's certificate of competency valid on ships of any tonnage when navigating the great lakes or, in the case of a pilot to be registered for the pilotage of the St. Lawrence river between St. Regis and lake Ontario, a pilot's licence valid for those waters;
(c)	he has served as master or as pilot on the waters concerned, while holding the appropriate master's certificate of competency or pilot's licence, for such a period as may be required by the Minister of Transport;
(d)	he is of good character, physically healthy and personally suitable;
(e)	he passes successfully such examination as may be required by the Minister of Transport.
(2)	Registration as a pilot may, at the discretion of the Minister of Transport, be for a limited time and may be renewed from time to time.
(3)	Registration may be revoked where the Minister of Transport is satisfied that the

services of a registered pilot are unsatisfactory by reason of incompetency or misconduct or in case of physical incapacity.
Qualifications for "other officers". (1) a person shall not act as an officer required by subparagraph (ii) of paragraph (b) of subsection (1) of section 375B of the Canada Shipping Act to be on board a vessel while navigating waters other than those designated pursuant to paragraph (a) of subsection (1) of section 375C of the said act unless:
(a)	he is a member of the regular complement of the vessel;
(b)	he holds a certificate of competency as master, for foreign-going voyages, issued by or accepted by the government of the country in which the ship is registered;
(c)	he has made at least two round voyages into those waters of the great lakes basin for which he is to be qualified;
(d)	he has a good working knowledge of the rules of the road for the great lakes;
(e)	he has a sufficient command of the English language for the effective use of the radiotelephone; and
(f)	he holds a document issued by the Canadian Department of Transport certifying that he has been examined and found duly qualified.
